       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg/day. I don't know of any protocol or indication that supports it, and it could cause serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac arrhythmia. You haven't given a clinical rationale, so I can't treat this as an intentional exception.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Tell me the dose you want, up to 200 mg/day. For a new start, that would usually be 25\u201350 mg once daily.\n- **Discuss it with pharmacy or the attending.** If there is a real reason for a dose this high, such as a specific protocol, they can review it. I can enter the order with that rationale in the note once it's documented.\n- **Check the source.** If the order came from a transcription or a verbal order, it's worth confirming it with the prescriber.\n\nLet me know which you'd like, and I'll enter the order right away."
      }
